pre-shell and post-shell stamped the cwd of the hook input, so a shell command that cd'd into another repository, or ran git -C on it, was not stamped where it made its changes; two commits today came out all human with their reasons dropped. agit-hook now works out the directory from a leading cd or git -C, as the removed commit_dir did, resolving relative paths and ~ against cwd and falling back to cwd, and uses it for both begin and end. The tests cover absolute, relative, quoted, ~ and git -C cases and the fallbacks.
